      "side": 1,
      "message": "From AI:\n\n1. Regex False Positives (Word Boundaries) In polygerrit-ui/app/models/chat/context-item-util.ts, the keywordRegex checks for the presence of keywords like \"bug\" or \"fix\" anywhere in the line:\n\nTypeScript\nconst keywordRegex \u003d\n  /(?:bug|fix|issue|fixed|fixes|bugfix|google-bug-id|cts-coverage-bug|crs-fixed)/i;\nBecause this regex lacks word boundaries (\\b), it will match words that contain these keywords.\n\nScenario: A commit message contains \"Enable debugging for feature X 12345678\".\n\nResult: The regex matches \"bug\" inside \"debugging\", and \"12345678\" is incorrectly flagged as a bug ID.\n\nFix: Wrap the keywords in word boundaries or ensuring they appear at the start of the line/word.\n\nTypeScript\n// Example fix\nconst keywordRegex \u003d\n  /\\b(?:bug|fix|issue|fixed|fixes|bugfix|google-bug-id|cts-coverage-bug|crs-fixed)\\b/i;",
